    "description": "Cross-binding conformance for esm-spec \u00a76.6.2 'Shaped values' and the \u00a711.4 state-free-array-observed `ic` right-hand side: a SHAPED variable carries its whole field as INLINE ARRAY DATA \u2014 a row-major nested JSON array on its `default`, in a test's `parameter_overrides`, or in a test's `initial_conditions` (\u00a76.3) \u2014 and an `ic` may be seeded from a state-free array observed resolvable in the \u00a76.6.5 build-time evaluation scope. Before this, all three positions were `number`-only in `esm-schema.json` and a `const`-gather `ic` RHS was rejected at build, so a \u00a76.6 inline test could not supply a SHAPED input at all: the only escape was a test-injected rewrite-rule library (\u00a79.7.10) lowering a rewrite-target op to an inline `const` column \u2014 one generated `.esm` per test \u2014 which is what a column-physics component replaying a Fortran kernel dump had to do for every regime, because its inputs ARE columns (\u03b8, q_v, u, v, p, dz, K profiles). Each fixture is ONE shared component whose regimes are ordinary tests of the same document. Non-vacuity is structural rather than incidental: the `declared_defaults` / `rank2_declared_default` half reads the array-valued DEFAULTS and the override half replaces them, so a binding that dropped array data entirely fails the first half instead of passing both on zeros; and every fixture re-asserts a state seeded by a `const` gather the overrides do not touch, so an override leaking into the build-time array scope fails rather than silently agreeing. The RANK-2 fixture's axes have different extents (lev=2, col=3) and pairwise-distinct element values, which pins the row-major nesting order element-for-element: a binding that read the authored array in column-major order, or flattened it against its own state-vector order, disagrees on every off-diagonal cell. Julia is the reference binding; its `run_inline_tests` minted both goldens.",
    "reference_binding": "julia",
    "bindings_required": [
        "julia",
        "python",
        "rust"
    ],
    "scope_excluded": {
        "go": "rewrite-only port; no makearray lowering / simulator / inline PDE-test runner",
        "typescript": "rewrite-only port; no makearray lowering / simulator / inline PDE-test runner"
    },
    "integrators": {
        "julia": {
            "algorithm": "Tsit5",
            "reltol": 1e-12,
            "abstol": 1e-14
        },
        "python": {
            "method": "RK45",
            "rtol": 1e-12,
            "atol": 1e-14
        },
        "rust": {
            "solver": "Erk",
            "reltol": 1e-12,
            "abstol": 1e-14
        }
    },
    "tolerances": {
        "assertion_rtol": 1e-09,
        "assertion_atol": 1e-11
    },
